Jeff Plum wrote:
> 
> Redhat's documentation says 6.2 is incompatible with the AS 4100.  Does
> anyone know of a LINUX OS that is ported to the AS 4100?

The component of an operating system that does most of the talking to hardware
is the kernel. As you may know, the kernel is the same across all linux
distributions, so it's fairly likely that if redhat is incompatable, there
arn't any different linux distro's that are. However, according to the
NetBSD/Alpha page at

http://www.netbsd.org/Ports/alpha

they support the 4100. Even though it's not exactly what you asked for, it
still might be a worthwhile option.

