On Sat, 29 Jul 2000 18:05:18 GMT, Neoklis <neoklis@my-deja.com> wrote:
>
>I wonder what sort of a good sound card is compatible with a UP1000.
>I would like a PCI wavetable card, if possible similar to Creative
>Soundblaster 32.

Somewhere I think I heard that a Soundblaster Live! will work on
a UP1000.  However, I am told by the support folks at API
(Alpha-Processor Inc) that a Live! does _not_ work on a UP2000.
At least on the UP2000, the Ensoniq AudioPCI works with the ALSA
drivers (on PCI bus 0).  I'm sure happier now that my card is
working in my UP2000.  :-)

The ALSA drivers are good, but on machines with multiple PCI
buses, they require the card be on the first bus (bus 0).  If the
UP1000 only has one PCI bus, this would be a non-issue.  I am
told the ALSA folks will be getting a UP2000 and I think a UP1000
to use for driver development, so maybe the PCI bus issue will
eventually be solved.

The commercial OSS-based drivers from 4Front don't appear to work
any better than the free ALSA drivers, at least for a UP2000.
Also, 4Front will be removing Alpha support starting this fall.
(I paid for the 4Front drivers, but they could never get them to
work with the second PCI bus on my UP2000, so I wrote off the
loss and went with ALSA.)

You might check with the support folks at API to see if they can
give you a list of cards that work in the UP1000.
(Customer.Support@alpha-processor.com is their email address.)

Good luck,

Robert Riches
richesr1@inetarena.com



