I am running a Voodoo3 3000 on my UP2000.  I don't remember where
I read it, but I recall reading an instruction that the graphics
card must be on the first PCI bus (bus 0).  I have used mine in
the top slot and in the third slot.  I'm running a (basically)
stock Redhat 6.1 system with XFree version 3.3.5-17 for most of
the RPMs.  The only thing I had to do to make the Voodoo card
work was switch to the SVGA driver.  I have not done any fancy 2D
or 3D animation, just conventional X stuff.  The BTTV WinTV card
does works (at least the visual portion) with the Voodoo.

