boot the CD, not the floppy...

boot dqa0 -fi /kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0  expert text"

or if you must the floppy

boot dva0 -fi vmlinux.gz "root=/dev/scd0 expert text"

both use the CD as root so make sure the CD is installed in the reader
before booting.

check out
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/

for the latest smp kernels..


for install guides

http://www.compaq.com/alphaserver/linux/install_guide.html

follow any SRM install (ES40) only diff is the device names ES40 uses ide
CD,  4x00 uses scsi


Finally

http://www.linuxalpha.compaq.com/jumpstart/

is a bootable CD available as an ISO, which will setup your ALPHA SRM,
partition the drives and get it ready to install linux. All current dists
are supported...


