Hi,

I had problems with hwclock incorrectly reading the cmos clock and
setting system time to bizzare values. After consultation with the
maintainer of hwclock, we found out that the fault was due to hwclock
not recognising the UP1000 as a "funky-toy" machine. The
fix was to supply the -F (--funky-toy) option to hwclock.

I wonder if other UP1000 owners had this fault. It was not known
to the vendors of my machine or the maintainer of hwclock.

TIA


-- 
Regards

Neoklis Kyriazis



