Wow, I have exactly the same hardware and exactly the same problem.

The only thing I do differently is compile a new kernel while logged
in remotely in the hopes that using it will prevent lockups in the
future.  So far, I've been doing this for 6 months.  It's the only
reason I ever reboot.  I may try >= 2.2.17pre10 as suggested but
it hasn't worked in the past, so I don't have my hopes up.

You may try occasionally logging out to hopefully clear up a memory
leak, but it's awful tough to prove that it does anything.

BTW, while logged in remotely, I su to root and can then start X back
up.  It works fine while using it, but locks the card back up when I
log out.  I suppose you could avoid rebooting for quite a while that
way, but what about the unfortunate people who don't have a second
box?  Their system is just hosed.

Does anyone know of any way to reinitialize a video card with the
machine running?  Like ifconfig but for video cards?

