X-Deja-AN: 650374599
Organization: CYTANET
X-Sender: root@up1000.nkk.home
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

Hi

I was having problems with the hwclock command occasionally
misreading the cmos clock on my UP1000 and setting the system 
time to odd values. After consultation with the maintainer and
some debugging runs, I learned that the falt was hwclock not
recognising the UP1000 (likely the UP2000 as well) as a "funky-toy"
machine. The fix is to use the -F ( --funky-toy ) option in the
boot script that uses hwclock to set system time.

I am posting this as neither the vendor nor the maintainer of
hwclock were informed about this, so presumably there may be some
other UP1000 owners that have the same problem.

-- 
Regards

Neoklis Kyriazis




