OK,

    Select srm from Alphabios cmos advanced setup.

after the f10 to save the srm unix console selection, power cycle the box..

if the post count-down stalls, try pressing the reset button on the box a
few times.. it may drop into the console prompt.  if not, power down the
system and  remove the battery, leave it out for a long while,  this is to
insure it really forgets.  try 1-2 hrs. It will remember for a while after
the battery is removed (so the batt can be replaced without losing settings.

when the battery is reinstalled, the console should default to serial port
0. and any changes made by isacfg will revert to factory defaults.

JJ

