To get back to SRM, there is a menu in ARC that allows you to choose an
alternative operating system. There are three selections and from memory
you choose the middle one. From SRM it isn't too difficult to upgrade
the firmware if you have a tftp server and a working network. I've never
done it from floppy because I never got a floppy drive :-(

> I was wondering if anyone had any ideas on how to get started with either
> upgrading the firmware so that I get the SRM console, or installing either
> Linux or NetBSD on it. 

You don't need to upgrade the firmware to get to SRM, there is an
ARC menu option that does it. You must reboot once you select that
menu option. You may need to upgrade the firmware if your SRM does
not support features that you need (some of the old ones won't
support IDE discs for example).

