If you have not done so already you will probably want to read 
http://www.alphalinux.org - especially the docs. 

Last time I installed Red Hat (long time ago) there was one ramdisk 
image for all Alphas. You can find a mirror of Red Hat for Alpha at 
ftp://ftp.alphalinux.org/mirrors/redhat/redhat-6.2/

The ramdisk image is at 
ftp://ftp.alphalinux.org/mirrors/redhat/redhat-6.2/images/ramdisk.img

The AS800, aka corelle, is not supported by milo. So you will have to 
kiss NT good bye and change the firmware to SRM. See 
ftp://ftp.alphalinux.org/pub/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/systypes.txt for a 
list of Alphas and milo/SRM support. 


You may also want to subscribe to the following mailing lists: 

Red Hat's Alpha list: axp-list@redhat.com / send subscription request 
to axp-list-request@redhat.com with "subscribe" in the subject line. 

AlphaLinux.org's hardware list: visit 
http://lists.alphalinux.org/mailman/listinfo/axp-hardware

