Hello Devin!

DB> I have an Alpha AXP/150 (AKA Jensen) and I've been trying to get
Linux
DB> installed on it.  I understand that I need to have SRM Firmware
version 1.7
DB> or higher.  How do I tell what SRM version I have?  When I turn the
machine
DB> on I get two version numbers.

This ist the most recent firmware; you can use it without any change
with windows NT. For Linux, however, this is not the best choice, it
limits at least the number of useable graphics adapters. The ELSA
Winner 1000 ISA/EISA will run in ISA mode only, for example. I've heard
rumours of probloeems with aboot, too, but didn't test this due to my
graphics card.

DB> Alpha AXP System ROM Version 1.9 and
DB> Alpha AXP SRM Firmware Version 34a

DB> 34a seem a long way off from 1.7  Is this my SRM version or is it
the 1.9?

Actually there are two firmwares in the file, the ARC and the SRM
console. The correct numbers for you are "1.7" and "32f".

If anybody is successfully running another version, please let me know.

To the best of my knowledge, installing exactly this firmware should be
the first thing you do, at least as soon as you are experiencing any
problem during the installation process. Both Linux and NT will run
perfectly well with it. The 1.9 has got a better language support, as I
remember, but that's a feature you'll hardly need.

Regards, Christoph



