make boot
make modules
make modules_install
cp System.map /boot/System.map-kernel.version.number
cp arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz /boot/vmlinuz-kernel.version.number
cd /boot
ln -sf /boot/System.map-kernel.version.number System.map
ln -sf /boot/vmlinuz-kernel.version.number vmlinuz


Make xconfig is usually broken (maybe CML2 from ESR will help)
so use make config instead.  Make oldconfig on an old .config
file is usually the way I'd recommend it.  Make bzImage doesn't
mean anything at all on an alpha, it's just for x86's.

So, you still booting MILO off the floppy?  No big deal, just
make a back up floppy and try not to boot the machine all that
often.  You don't absolutely need the DOS partition.

Hope this helps,

Tony Hammitt


