Markus Rahlff,

	I am running a (ok, several) Alpha Stations with the 3-com 'Tornado'
card.  This is the 3c905c that you mentioned in your previous post.  It
is supported using the 3c59x.c driver.  In the same machine, I also have
a DC21143 Tulip card that came with the machine.  Both are working
wonderfully.  I have compiled the driver in the 2.2.14 through 2.2.16
kernels and have not had any problems.  You can enable this driver by
choosing the following driver in the kernel configuration: 
[*] 3c590/3c900 series (592/595/597) "Vortex/Boomerang" support  
Note that you may alternately load this driver as a module with no
problems.

For more information on building a kernel on an alpha, check out
alphalinux.org.  There is a how-to on building a kernel (note that this
process is slightly different from ix86 kernel build).

good luck

Matt Lee
