> I am dealing with large files, I would like to know
> the size limit of a single file on alpha version of
> linux.

AlphaLinux does not have the 2 GB limit that x86 Linux currently has
-- not only is "long" 64 bits, which fixes the library interface
issue, but ext2fs does support that.

On x86 Linux, you can get the same effect by using the LFS routines
like read64 etc.

