I think netscape on alpha Linux is the Tru64 binary, so your kernel will
need to support ECOFF/AOUT binaries.

Use make config (menuconfig or whatever) to configure this support (I
think its called; CONFIG_BINFMT_AOUT=y) into your home-brew kernel.

Also, I seem to remember someone posting on the axp-list that 2.2.16 had a
feature that stops netscape from working on alpha. So if you're trying to
use 2.2.16, check the AXP list archive at;

http://www.lib.uaa.alaska.edu/axp-list/

Actually reading your post again, maybe you already have
CONFUG_BINFMT_AOUT set so perhaps you are seeing the 2.2.16 feature ?

Addy.


